  "build": {
    "buildCommand": "cd /Users/ak/Addon/aoc-erp\ngit add apps/web/lib/rbac.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/accounting.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/bom.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/delivery.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/drawing.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/gst.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/inventory.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/invoice.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/purchase.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/qc.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/quotation.ts apps/web/server/trpc/routers/workOrder.ts\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix: enforce RBAC on financial/operational mutations (was tenantProcedure-only)\n\nEvery mutation outside CRM (leads/clients/architects/projects, already\ncorrectly gated) only checked tenantProcedure -- logged in + same tenant,\nno role check. Any authenticated tenant member, including 'viewer', could\ndelete invoices, void posted journal entries, delete purchase orders,\ndelete QC inspection records, etc.\n\nMapped each mutation to the existing lib/rbac.ts permission it semantically\nbelongs to (MANAGE_FINANCE, MANAGE_PRODUCTION, MANAGE_INVENTORY, CREATE_PO,\nCREATE_QUOTE, MANAGE_DELIVERY, MANAGE_DRAWINGS/VIEW_DRAWINGS). Added\nVIEW_QC/MANAGE_QC (didn't exist) so production_staff can record inspections\non the floor while only managers can delete inspection records.\n\nTwo deliberate exceptions to a strict \"most restrictive\" default: quotation\nupdateStatus uses CREATE_QUOTE not APPROVE_QUOTE (it also covers routine\ndraft->sent transitions salespeople do themselves), and work-order\nupdateStatus uses VIEW_PRODUCTION not MANAGE_PRODUCTION (advancing\ncutting->grinding->...->dispatch is production_staff's core floor job, not\na manager-only action).\n\nVerified: 13/13 permission-map assertions pass (unit-level, allow/deny per\nrole); tsc clean.\nEOF\n)\"\ngit push origin phase-0-foundation 2>&1",
    "testCommand": "cd /Users/ak/Addon/aoc-erp\ngit diff --cached --stat | tail -5\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\ntest: add automated test suite for AI extraction and file upload workflows\n\nNo automated tests existed anywhere in this repo — every prior \"E2E test\"\nwas manual, interactive, and left no regression capability. This is why the\nDWG upload bug and the purchase-doc PDF bug (fixed in the two preceding\ncommits) both went undetected until specifically hunted for.\n\n- tests/unit: mocked-Anthropic tests for @aoc/ai's content-block branching\n  (image vs document) — the exact bug class behind both fixes\n- tests/integration: real Supabase Storage + real tRPC router calls\n  (createCaller) against an ephemeral per-suite tenant, mocked model calls —\n  drawing upload/extract, purchase doc scan, business card + GST cert scan\n  (all 4 entity routers), proposal PDF structural validity, QR code\n  generation. Covers positive/negative/boundary/malformed/RBAC/rate-limit\n  cases, and always asserts final persisted state, not just \"didn't throw\"\n- tests/live (opt-in, `pnpm test:live`, not part of default `pnpm test`):\n  real Anthropic API calls against real fixtures, for actual extraction\n  accuracy — costs tokens, so kept out of the default fast/free suite\n- tests/fixtures: genuine files in real formats from public sources (never\n  renamed-extension stand-ins) — see tests/fixtures/README.md for full\n  provenance, including why the business-card/GST-cert images are safe to\n  commit (a historical public artifact and a public institution's\n  legally-public registration, not private data)\n\nEphemeral test tenants clean up their own DB rows, Storage objects, and\nauth users after each run — verified zero leftover state post-suite.\n\n63 tests pass by default; 4 additional live tests pass against the real API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"",
    "lintCommand": "pnpm lint",
    "devCommand": "pnpm dev",
